      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T20:47:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would take a while for Dawn extension to finish. It\u0027s currently handled by our Intel partners anw. Implementating in Dawn is also more complicated due to having to serve general users. It has to support multiple color attachments. It has to add some rules for render pipeline\u0027s compatibility due to Vulkan\u0027s specific details.\n\nOn the other hands, I\u0027m intending to use this emulation on devices with desktop GPUs (mostly D3D). e.g. D3D11 doesn\u0027t have any concept of render passes. Load/Store are noop. So having multiple render passes with Load/Store does nothing detrimental at all. So having this emulation here would be the same as what the extension in Dawn would do. But we can test it in practice earlier. D3D12 does have render passes. However D3D12 as a graphite\u0027s backend still has a long way to go. So it\u0027s not worth to wait for its extension\u0027s implementation in Dawn to complete IMO.\n\nOn most platforms with tiled GPUs (mac, android), we already have Transient Attachment implemented so neither this emulation nor partial resolve are needed.\nSo IMO even if we kept this emulation and used it on devices without `TransientAttachment` (they are mostly non-tiled GPUs currently), the perf would not be affected much.",
      "parentUuid": "2849fb02_7d642faa",
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
