      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T19:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure we want to commit to actually doing multiple render passes here. I believe we can take this code path if we are running WASM+WebGPU and don\u0027t have access to the various dawn extensions. This could easily be on platforms that would regress performance-wise or run into correctness issue (but perhaps not, since transient attachments are one of those extensions, so loading and storing is possible still).\n\nIf I\u0027m understanding this correctly, we are no longer copying the resolve texture into a separate single-channel texture. Before we would do: 1) blit (resolve-\u003ecopy), render (draw w/ copy, ..., resolve) and now we do: 1) render (draw resolve to color) 2) render (..., store color) 3) render (draw color to resolve).\n\nIf we aren\u0027t resolving in the main render pass, I don\u0027t think we need to have a separate intermediate render pass at the start. There shouldn\u0027t be any more restriction of just sampling the resolve texture at the start of the main render pass.  It would mean that the blit-as-draw pipeline needs to handle depth/stencil attachments as part of its key though.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 463,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 469,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71893b08_6dfd97bd",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T20:47:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The old loadResolve emulation path was intended as an interim solution. Most of the platforms with tiled GPUs already have DawnLoadResolve extension implemented anw.\n\nIn this CL if we change the emulation such that we have 3 render passes with multiple Load/Store steps. On D3D11, these are noop, so it won\u0027t change much in term of perf.\n\nI understand this might affect WASM because DawnLoadResolve is not exposed there. But I thought WASM is low priority for now. Or at least, the best way would be better if Dawn decided to expose the DawnLoadResolve extension in WASM. If you want, I can keep the old emulation path for now. In addition to the new partial resolve emulation\u0027s path.\n\nThough merging the first load to the main render pass also makes sense, will need to keep the depth/stencil as part of the key. We can use 64 bits key for that.",
      "parentUuid": "aa49afa4_b672aae1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 463,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 469,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3c4b221_8cc9335c",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T20:13:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WASM isn\u0027t a high priority, but we do have active clients that use it so ideally we don\u0027t set it back too much. In this case, the trade off is that we might hurt performance but would lower memory usage, which they would probably appreciate.\n\nThe new skgpu::TextureFormat enum fits into 8 bits, so I don\u0027t think we will need to increase the key size to 64 bits either but I wouldn\u0027t worry about that right away. I think first if we can get a sense of performance with the 2-pass vs. 3-pass approaches on both D3D11 and on Metal (with transient attachments disabled to simulate WASM path on a tiling GPU).\n\nI agree that hopefully we can expose transient attachments and load-resolve extensions in WASM. I would like to only keep one emulation path, so we should just work out exactly how we want the new one to behave.",
      "parentUuid": "71893b08_6dfd97bd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 463,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 469,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01ea843c_f8c23888",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 469,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T15:57:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have made this CL 2-pass only for now. The 1st blit will be part of the main render pass.\n\nI tested 3-pass vs 2-pass with nanobench\u0027s replays on M1 (transient attachment disabled). 3-pass is generally a bit slower. Most notable is mobi_youtube test, 3-pass is 17% slower than 2-pass.\n\nOn D3D11, both have similar perf.",
      "parentUuid": "d3c4b221_8cc9335c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 463,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 469,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
