        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T20:13:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we are rendering U/V without AA, we want the depth attachment to be `GetApproxSize(Y dims)`.\n\nIf we are rendering U/V with AA, and we have the load extension so we aren\u0027t using a separate render pass, we will want the depth attachment to be `GetApproxSize(Y dims)`. The color attachment, though, can be `GetApproxSize(U/V dims)`, right?\n\nIf we are rendering U/V with AA and no extension, then both the color and depth attachments can be `GetApproxSize(U/V dims)` because they won\u0027t be resolved. And the blitAsDraw into the multiplanar target will use an internal renderpass configured to have no depth attachment at all.\n\nIf we just passed in `colorAttachment-\u003edimensions()` here, `getDepthAttachmentDimensions()` won\u0027t have to separately call `GetApproxSize` since it\u0027ll be `GetApproxSize(U/V dims)`.  Multiplying that by 2 to get the Y size almost always works out correctly.  For every input size \u003e 8px, 2*GetApproxSize(sz) \u003d\u003d GetApproxSize(2*sz).  For sz \u003c\u003d 8px, 2*GetApproxSize(sz) returns 32 instead of 16 but that shouldn\u0027t be problematic since that\u0027s still larger than the Y plane size.\n\nThe only downside to not providing the renderpass sample count to `getDepthAttachmentDimensions` is that when we are rendering MSAA to U/V but don\u0027t have the load extension, we would use `GetApproxSize(y dims)` instead of the smaller `GetApproxSize(uv dims)`. I\u0027m inclined to keep the function simple and less coupled to the multipass configurations of a specific backend when it\u0027s pretty unlikely for multiplanar rendering to trigger AA anyways.",
      "parentUuid": "b131b52a_8c41150a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 181,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "b2740cd1cc06998eaa340fc6fcb04af43e10475c",
